    "everyArtifactHashNamedInThisDecision": true,
    "why": "The owner named these three digests and every full artifact hash. Binding to all of them means the approval cannot survive a regenerated batch, a re-inspected page set, or a re-rendered artifact: any of those moves a digest, and the loader refuses rather than carrying the approval onto bytes nobody approved."
  },
  "acceptedVisualObservations": {
    "accepted": true,
    "requiresAnotherArtifactLoop": false,
    "observations": [
      "A short block sometimes takes a page of its own.",
      "The document-check table names court-facing documents in English on the Spanish page.",
      "The two Mississippi routes still share their guide wording, and now differ in their court documents.",
      "The renderer wraps on a kerned measurement and draws unkerned text."
    ],
    "ownerStatement": "The occasional short standalone page is cosmetic; English titles for actual English court documents in the Spanish checklist are intentional identification aids; the shared Mississippi guide correctly explains both statutory branches while the filed documents now derive the correct branch automatically; and the measured 2.32pt text-block overrun remains roughly 43.7pt inside the physical page edge, with no clipping and the affected pages visually inspected. These observations are not reasons to alter this approval."
  },
