  "ownerInstruction": "OWNER DECISION — APPROVED. Record one new owner-decision artifact approving the exact 18 artifact entries: the 15 Item 13B artifacts plus the current three-artifact Mississippi non-conviction successor set. Bind the decision to commit ed7356a733b5f47976e012c9ba386f0a021057ca, Item 13B batch SHA-256 5166d9159e7d4ff111c36a264b224d7760e47356ee119cdefa6ac3abe44c82ee, visual-review SHA-256 bd248b2aa8fb84e57893f4c5695733816fb9db24eb20d1c693edd8a97b0f1c29, and every full artifact hash listed in this approval. This is exact-current-artifact approval, including the §7 guides and the route-derived Mississippi statutory branches. Preserve all earlier approvals and move records unedited. Supersede where appropriate; do not rewrite history. The four recorded visual observations are accepted as nonblocking for these exact artifacts and do not require another artifact loop. Regenerate the fulfillment registry, worker-static authority, runtime manifest and all existing verification controls. Before worker publication, confirm: the five Item 13B routes no longer have the current commercial artifact approval missing-proof; the MS non-conviction owner_decision mismatch is gone; the old MS approval still exists unchanged; no 'explained move' path can substitute for this new owner decision; any remaining hold is genuinely provider/publication or another pre-existing independent gate. If regeneration exposes a new substantive defect, stop on that defect. Do not re-pin around it. Then fast-forward the canonical integration branch to the resulting final candidate; this fast-forward is authorized. After canonical integration, publish the RCAP worker once using the existing workflow with integration_sha empty; worker publication is authorized for this candidate. Capture the immutable source SHA/image digest, regenerate the authority projection, and run the matching hosted/static acceptance checks. Production promotion, live charges, and any separate production deployment remain unauthorized."
